      },
      "lineNbr": 1645,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-06T15:21:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the host kernel should be the initiator of the `kvm_notify_vm_availability` and I wonder if we can do it separately (not on the back of a guest call but on a different hvc as we do with kvm_call_hyp_nvhe(__pkvm_notify_dying_guest_vm_avail). Maybe we can even re-use it and adjust the name accordingly. \n\nWe can try a couple of times to notify and if it didn\u0027t work, we bail out and don\u0027t handle guest-ffa at all for that VM. What do you think ?",
      "parentUuid": "6602d1cc_d14ad1fd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1645,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 1645,
        "endChar": 19
