    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29b64365_12fcd198",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 84
      },
      "lineNbr": 386,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-06T20:50:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure, as long as you don\u0027t make it conditional on `nr_busy`. There was a bug earlier where the availability messages wouldn\u0027t get sent from `__pkvm_reclaim_dying_guest_ffa_resources` if `nr_busy \u003d\u003d 0`.\n\nThere is one argument in favor of doing it separately: we only need to send the availability messages once, not once per page in a loop.\n\nOne minor note: an earlier patchset had the call in `__pkvm_start_teardown_vm` but got some feedback to move it out into its own function.",
      "parentUuid": "f480c25d_2b88498c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 379,
        "startChar": 0,
